WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.630
A window onto a London street.

2
00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:05.300
"Foggier yet, and colder."

3
00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.010
Then frost creeps over the glass.

4
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:10.220
Then firelight dances in it.

5
00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:12.680
Then, clear bright sun.

6
00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:17.540
And every time the sky shifts, the
man behind the window shifts too.

7
00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:21.030
So why does the weather
seem to follow Scrooge?

8
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.200
In this mission, you'll read
the story on two levels:

9
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.100
what happens, and what it stands for.

10
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.960
You'll open Dickens's toolkit, from
similes and lists to a narrator who speaks

11
00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.470
as if he's at your elbow.

12
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.390
And you'll step into the
Stave 1 fog, on Christmas Eve,

13
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.180
through "the palpable brown air".

14
00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:44.460
Your mission: explain why the
weather changes as Scrooge does.
